    AM["👁️ **HER PROOF, 14 JUL:** *'I was in Braai, and next moment I was in Butter Chicken. The moment I<br/>click the search box, I end up in Butter Chicken. So I cannot search Braai.'* **Spice does it too.**<br/><br/>🩸 **MEASURED — `core.js`:**<br/>**517:** `else if (S.viewingRecipe)             { content = recipeView(); }` ⬅️ **ASKED FIRST**<br/>**520:** `else if (S.screen==='search_results'){ content = searchResultsHTML(); }` ⬅️ **NEVER REACHED**<br/>**THE ROUTER ASKS *IS A RECIPE OPEN?* BEFORE IT ASKS *WHAT SCREEN?***<br/><br/>· `braai.js:28` → search pill sets `S.screen` — **and NEVER clears `S.viewingRecipe`.**<br/>· `spice.js:7982` → **IDENTICAL onclick. IDENTICAL OMISSION.**<br/>· `braai.js:27` → **the My Plan button RIGHT NEXT TO IT *does* clear it** *(`viewingRecipe:null`)*.<br/>· `core.js:399` → **the bottom-nav *does* clear it** *(`viewingRecipe:false`)* — **which is WHY the<br/>  bottom search works and the in-room pill does not.**<br/>⚖️ **Law 31 — IT WAS NEVER CLOSED ON THE WAY IN. The same disease as MF89.**<br/><br/>👁️ **AND THEN TINA PROVED IT IS NOT A SEARCH BUG AT ALL, 14 JUL:**<br/>🩸 ***'I Have Chicken is also sticky. I go out and back in, and the previous page — butternut<br/>muffins — is still the first thing I see.'*** **SHE NEVER TOUCHED A SEARCH BOX. THE TILE DOES IT.**<br/>📏 **CENSUS: 32 screen-changes across 11 files change `S.screen` WITHOUT clearing `S.viewingRecipe`.<br/>ONLY 3 DO IT RIGHT.** ⚖️ **Law 22 — that is a RISK LIST, NOT a bug list. DO NOT FIX 32 SITES.**<br/><br/>🏆🏆 **THE FIX IS ONE LINE — AND TINA ALREADY WROTE IT ONCE, IN JUNE.**<br/>**`core.js:489`, inside `draw()`:**<br/>```if(screenChanged) S._searchOwner = null;   // MF59-B · the QUERY belongs to its screen```<br/>**NOBODY EVER DID THE SAME FOR THE RECIPE. ADD ONE LINE BESIDE IT:**<br/>```if(screenChanged) S.viewingRecipe = null;  // MF95 · the RECIPE belongs to its screen too```<br/>⚖️ **Law 33 — `draw()` IS THE FLOOR. EVERY NAV PATH LANDS THERE.**<br/>⚖️ **Law 35 — LIFT IT, DON'T INVENT IT. NO `openSectionSearch()`. NOTHING ELSE MOVES.**<br/>✅ **SAFE — VERIFIED: `openRecipe()` NEVER CHANGES THE SCREEN.** A recipe is an OVERLAY on the<br/>screen it was opened from. **So a screen-change with a recipe still open is ALWAYS stale. Always.**<br/>⛔ **DO NOT reorder lines 517/520. Recipe-first is CORRECT — it IS an overlay. The bug was that<br/>NOBODY CLOSED IT.**<br/><br/>🏆 **AND COMMIT 2 — `goBack()` step (4), `core.js:425`:**<br/>```if(S.screen !== 'home'){ bottomBarGo('home'); return; }``` ⬅️ **THE BACK BUTTON, ALL THREE DAYS.**<br/>🩸 **`S.searchPrevScreen` IS ALREADY SET by braai.js, spice.js AND liveSearch(). `goBack()` HAS<br/>NEVER ONCE READ IT.** ✅ **ONE LINE → kills MF64 + MF65 + MF72.** ⚠️ **HYPOTHESIS, not measured.<br/>If Back still misbehaves after it — STOP and read `NAV_KEYS`.** ⚖️ **Law 22.**<br/><br/>📄 **`BRIEF_MF95.md` IS WRITTEN. TWO COMMITS. TWO LINES. ⚖️ Law 4 turned 12 bugs into 2 lines.**"]
  end

  subgraph TWOENG["🩸 **THERE ARE TWO SEARCH ENGINES IN TINZA. THEY DO NOT AGREE.** *(14 Jul)*"]
    TE["⚖️ **Law 39 FIRED ON CLAUDE, 14 JUL. HE MEASURED THE WRONG ENGINE AND PREDICTED 0 HITS.<br/>TINA'S FINGERS SAID 9. HER FINGERS WERE RIGHT.**<br/><br/>· **ENGINE 1 · `allRecipes({text:})`** *(`index.js:489`)* — plain `indexOf` on `searchText`.<br/>· **ENGINE 2 · `tinzaAllSearch()`** *(`utils.js:132`)* — word-start regex, **AND it searches every<br/>  version's `name` + `feel` + ingredients.** ⬅️ **THIS IS THE ONE THE APP ACTUALLY USES.**<br/>⚖️ **SAMENESS — ONE APP MUST HAVE ONE SEARCH. THIS IS A ROOT, NOT A LEAF.**<br/><br/>💀 **AND IT EXPLAINS THE 9 MEAT DISHES.** Butter Chicken's Paneer version's **`feel`** reads:<br/>*'the same butter gravy around golden cubes of paneer — the much-loved **vegetari**an…'*<br/>🩸 **THE WORD 'VEGETARIAN' IS IN A MARKETING SENTENCE. NOT A TAG.** The match fires — and the<br/>card then shows **THE MEAT PARENT'S NAME.**<br/>👁️ **HER SCREENS:** Spaghetti Bolognese · Butter Chicken · Beef Chilli con Carne · Classic Bobotie ·<br/>**Greek Lamb Moussaka** — *all returned for the query `vegetarian`.*<br/>💀💀 **AND FOR `vegan`: MOROCCAN LAMB &amp; APRICOT TAGINE.** ⚖️ **THIS IS NOT SILENT WRONG.<br/>IT IS LOUD AND WRONG. A VEGAN ASKED TINZA A QUESTION AND TINZA HANDED HER LAMB.**<br/><br/>🏆 **BUT THE VERSIONS ARE TREASURE — DO NOT DELETE THEM.** *A paneer Butter Chicken and a<br/>vegan tagine are things **NYT COOKING DOES NOT HAVE.** They are a MOAT.*<br/>✅ **THE FIX:** tag the **VERSION** with a real `diet:` — and when the match is ON a version, the card<br/>must read **'Butter Chicken · Paneer version'**. **NEVER the meat name alone.**"]
  end

  subgraph CENSUS["📊 **THE CENSUS — `node tinza-census.js` · NEW, 14 JUL · READ-ONLY**"]
    CN["⚖️ **THE DOCTOR ASKS *'IS IT BROKEN?'* → RED or GREEN.**<br/>⚖️ **THE CENSUS ASKS *'HOW MUCH OF IT IS THERE?'* → A NUMBER.** ⚖️ **Law 36.**<br/>⚖️ **Law 42 — THE RATCHET. EVERY BUG YOU CLOSE ADDS A CHECK HERE. A bug the census catches<br/>cannot come back quietly. THE WALLS GET HIGHER. The bugs do not stop — the WALLS get higher.**<br/><br/>**IT COUNTS SIX THINGS TODAY:**<br/>**1 ·** Is the search instant? **2 ·** How many search engines are there? **3 ·** Can Tinza answer<br/>*'I am vegetarian'*? **4 ·** Is a diet being read out of a SENTENCE? **5 ·** Does every tool open<br/>empty? **6 ·** Does every room have a search box?<br/><br/>🩸 **WHAT IT FOUND THE FIRST TIME IT RAN:**<br/>· 🐌 **4,867 recalculations per keystroke** *(MF98)*<br/>· 🔀 **4 of 5 test queries give DIFFERENT answers from the two engines**<br/>· 🥬 **52% diet coverage · 8 rooms fully blind · TWO words for the same food**<br/>· 💀 **127 VEGAN recipes are invisible to the vegetarian filter** *(MF94-D — exact count)*<br/>· 💀 **13 MEAT recipes answer a vegetarian/vegan search** *(MF94-E — the full list is in the output)*<br/>· 🔴 **budget · ingredient · fourIngredients · mood — none open empty**<br/>· 🚨 **`budget.js` AND `tinyTummies.js` have NO `sectionHeader()` AT ALL — NEVER MIGRATED TO<br/>  v33.** *(Same disease as Spice.)* ⚖️ **Law 34.**<br/><br/>⚖️ **Law 39 FIRED ON THE CENSUS ITSELF, WITHIN THE HOUR:** its first run flagged `braai`,<br/>`worldkitchen`, `health` as missing a reset. **THEY ARE DOORS, NOT QUESTIONS.** The regex was<br/>too greedy. **FIXED. A LYING CENSUS IS WORSE THAN NO CENSUS.**"]
  end

  subgraph SLOW["🐌 **MF98 — THE SEARCH MAKES HER WAIT.** *(14 Jul · MEASURED)*"]
    SL["👁️ **TINA, 14 JUL:** *'I enter butternut, it takes a while, it's not instant.'*<br/><br/>📏 **MEASURED — `utils.js:154-155`, INSIDE the 2083-recipe loop:**<br/>```var nameN = _searchNorm(r.name); var baseHay = _searchNorm(r.searchText);```<br/>**PLUS every version's name + feel + ingredient list, re-normalised too.**<br/><br/>💀 **ONE KEYSTROKE ('butternut') = 27 ms · 4,867 RE-NORMALISATIONS.**<br/>💀 **TYPING THE WHOLE WORD = 204 ms · 38,487 RE-NORMALISATIONS.**<br/>🚨 **AND THIS BOX IS 4-6× FASTER THAN HER TABLET. MULTIPLY IT.**<br/>**Nothing is precomputed. She re-reads the entire cookbook for every letter.**<br/><br/>✅ **THE FIX IS FREE.** ⚖️ **Law 6 + Law 35 — `rec()` (`index.js:66`) ALREADY builds `searchText`<br/>ONCE, at boot. NORMALISE THERE TOO:** `r._hay` · `r._nameN` · `r._vhay[]`.<br/>**Then `tinzaAllSearch` is nothing but regex tests. NEAR-INSTANT. NO NEW PLUMBING.**<br/>*(And it deletes the version-prose problem's cost at the same time — one pass, not 2083.)*"]
  end

