  subgraph SAMENESS["✨ **MF99 — THE SEARCH CARD THROWS AWAY WHAT IT ALREADY HAS** *(14 Jul · TINA SPOTTED IT)*"]
    SM["👁️ **TINA, 14 JUL:** *'what I like about I Have Chicken is, they all have times.'*<br/>**SHE WAS PAYING A COMPLIMENT. IT IS A BUG REPORT.**<br/><br/>| | ⏱️ time | 🌍 cuisine |<br/>| 🐔 **I Have Chicken** | ✅ 35 min | ✅ South African |<br/>| 🔍 **Search** | ❌ nothing | ❌ just 'Family Meals' |<br/>**SAME RECIPES. SAME INDEX. TWO RENDERERS.** ⚖️ **SAMENESS — HER #1 RULE. Search breaks it.**<br/><br/>📏 **MEASURED — a real search hit for `cheese` carries, RIGHT NOW:**<br/>```time=35 · cuisine=American · kcal=580 · costPP=30```<br/>🩸 **ALL OF IT IS ALREADY IN THE INDEX. `renderSearchResults` (`utils.js:260`) BINS IT.**<br/>⚖️ **Law 35 — NOTHING TO BUILD. ONE RENDERER. ONE LINE.**<br/><br/>✅ **THE CARD SHOULD READ:** *Creamy Mac &amp; Cheese · Family Meals · ⏱️ 35 min · American*<br/>**+ 💰 R30 pp — PRO ONLY, via the shared `costLine()`.** *(kcal too — nutrition = Pro, 7 Jul.)*<br/><br/>🩸 **AND IT FOUND A CONTENT GAP: 634 of 2083 recipes (30%) HAVE NO TIME AT ALL.**<br/>⚖️ **PROPOSED LAW 44 AGAIN — NO TIME → RENDER NOTHING. NEVER AN EMPTY `⏱️ —`.**<br/>**NO COST → NO PADLOCK. A lock must have something behind it.**"]
