  subgraph SOUL["✨ **`/tinza` — TINZA_STANDARD.md · WHO TINZA IS. RULED 14 JUL.**"]
    SO["👁️ **TINA, 14 JUL:** *'We should make a `/` for what Tinza is like and stands for.'*<br/><br/>| trigger | the question it answers |<br/>| `/wow` | **is this RECIPE good enough?** *(the food)* |<br/>| `/bug` | **is this BROKEN?** *(the code)* |<br/>| 🆕 **`/tinza`** | **does this SOUND like Tinza?** *(the soul)* |<br/>⚖️ **Law 23 — A CARD CAN PASS `/wow` AND STILL FAIL `/tinza`. That is exactly what it is for.**<br/><br/>🩸 **THE ONE-LINE TEST:** **READ IT ALOUD. IF IT SOUNDS LIKE A DATABASE, IT FAILS.<br/>IF IT SOUNDS LIKE A FRIEND WHO CAN COOK, IT PASSES.**<br/><br/>**THE NINE — each with a TEST, because a standard you cannot test is a slogan:**<br/>**1 ·** 👩‍🍳 **A CHEF, NOT A SEARCH RESULT** — she is at the counter, not on a server<br/>**2 ·** 😊 **WARM · DRY · SOMETIMES FUNNY · NEVER TWEE** — not a mascot, not a cupcake with a face<br/>**3 ·** 🩸 **HONESTY ABOVE ALL — NO POTATO BOBOTIE** *(⚖️ Law 43 — the beating heart)*<br/>**4 ·** 🍲 **FIVE VERSIONS, NOT ONE** — the bobotie you can AFFORD, and the one for the vegetarian<br/>   daughter. **Nobody else does this. IT IS A MOAT.**<br/>**5 ·** 🥪 **BETTER THAN THE ONE SHE KNOWS BY HEART** — *the hardest rule.* **If she could have<br/>   Googled it in ten seconds, THE CARD HAS FAILED. Even a cheese sandwich.**<br/>**6 ·** ✨ **NOTHING ORDINARY — THERE IS ALWAYS A TWIST** 🏆 *(Tina: 'the one I love particularly')*<br/>   **NAME THE TWIST OUT LOUD. If you cannot, there isn't one.**<br/>**7 ·** 📖 **THE THING SHE DIDN'T KNOW** — trivia she would repeat while serving. **Never a lecture.**<br/>**8 ·** 🎯 **RELIABLE — IT WORKS THE FIRST TIME.** 🩸 *A friendly voice that gives you a flat cake is<br/>   not friendly. It is a liar with a nice accent.*<br/>**9 ·** 💰 **THE RAND IS ALWAYS HONEST.** Green = food. Gold = shop. **It is why R90 is not R50.**<br/><br/>🇿🇦 **UNDERNEATH ALL NINE: SHE IS FROM HERE.** *There is no English word for a koeksister.<br/>There is a koeksister.* **NYT Cooking will never speak Afrikaans. That is the whole market.**<br/><br/>🚨 **THE FIVE FAILURES IT CATCHES:** THE DATABASE · THE MASCOT · THE CONFIDENT LIE ·<br/>**THE GOOGLE CARD** · THE LECTURE"]
  end

  subgraph VARIETY["🎲 **MF101 — THE SAME FIVE RECIPES, FOREVER.** *(14 Jul · TINA RAISED IT)*"]
    VR["👁️ **TINA, 14 JUL:** *'we will always get new recipes… at 2,200 we can\'t rotate much, but at 4,000 I<br/>think we will.'*<br/><br/>🩸 **THE NUMBER IS NOT THE PROBLEM. SHE ALREADY HAS ENOUGH.**<br/>📏 **MEASURED: `chicken` returns 182 HITS. TINZA SHOWS 5. The other 177 will NEVER be seen** —<br/>not because the shelf is thin, but because `utils.js:187` does `hits.sort(score)` and **NOTHING ELSE.<br/>The same five, the same order, forever.**<br/>🏆 **SHE DOES NOT NEED 4,000 RECIPES TO FEEL FRESH. SHE NEEDS THE 2,083 SHE HAS TO STOP<br/>HIDING BEHIND THE SAME FIVE.**<br/><br/>🏆 **AND THE ENGINE IS ALREADY BUILT AND HAS NEVER BEEN CALLED.**<br/>**`index.js:439` — `balancedOrder()` — *\'deterministic VARIETY round-robin (L12 · NO ML)\'*.<br/>ZERO CALLERS. ANYWHERE.** ⚖️ **Law 35 — LIFT IT, DON\'T INVENT IT.**<br/><br/>⚠️ **BUT \'ROTATION\' IS THREE DIFFERENT THINGS. ONLY ONE IS SAFE:**<br/>**1 · VARIETY** *(one result set isn\'t 5 chicken dishes in a row — DETERMINISTIC, same query same<br/>   answer)* → ✅ **DO IT. Engine built. Costs nothing. No launch risk.**<br/>**2 · ROTATION** *(same question, different day, different food — needs a time seed)* → ⚠️ **CAREFUL.**<br/>   🩸 **⚖️ LAW 2 DEPENDS ON REPRODUCIBILITY. IF RESULTS SHUFFLE, SHE CANNOT SCREENSHOT A BUG<br/>   AND PROVE IT.** *(A vegan gets a lamb tagine — and cannot make it happen again.)*<br/>**3 · FRESHNESS** *(\'new this week\')* → 📅 **THAT IS \'TINZA\'S WEEK\'. Already on the board. DELUXE.<br/>   A CONTENT JOB, NOT CODE.**<br/><br/>🚨 **THE RED LINE:** ⚖️ **Law 20 — `_fourCache` IS THE BUSINESS MODEL. Same fridge = ONE API<br/>call, ever. IF THE TINZA CHEF ROTATES, EVERY RE-SEARCH COSTS REAL RANDS.**<br/>**ROTATION IS FOR TINZA\'S OWN RECIPES. NEVER FOR THE CHEF.**<br/><br/>💡 **PROPOSED INSTEAD OF SILENT SHUFFLING: A BUTTON. 🎲 *\'Show me something else.\'***<br/>**She controls it. It is reproducible. No hidden state.** *And it is MORE delightful than a shuffle,<br/>because she ASKED and Tinza HAD MORE TO GIVE.* ⚖️ **`/tinza` rule 4 — five versions, not one.**<br/>👁️ **TINA TO RULE. NOT A LAUNCH BLOCKER. The VARIETY pass (1) is free — take it now.**"]
  end

  subgraph TRINITY["💰 **MF102 — THE TRINITY. 'EACH DISH NEEDS A COST.'** *(Tina, 14 Jul — MEASURED)*"]
    TR["👁️ **TINA ASKED: *'are we done with the costing bugs?'*** ⚖️ **Law 36 — I COUNTED. THE ANSWER IS NO.**<br/><br/>📏 **2083 RECIPES:** 🥬 **DIET 52%** · ⏱️ **TIME 70%** · 💰 **COST 74%**<br/>💀 **ONLY 1016 (49%) CARRY ALL THREE. 364 (17%) CARRY NONE OF THEM.**<br/><br/>💀 **532 RECIPES HAVE NO COST → INVISIBLE TO \'I\'VE GOT R100\'.**<br/>*(`index.js:483` — `if(r.costPP==null) return false`.)*<br/>**spice 184 · braai 92 · world 88 · beverages 66 · furry 62 · events 22 · tiny 18**<br/>📏 **A R100 BUDGET TODAY SEARCHES 1,506 RECIPES. NOT 2,083.**<br/><br/>🩸🩸 **AND BRAAI\'S COST IS NOT MISSING — IT IS BEING THROWN AWAY.**<br/>**`index.js:334` — the Braai adapter:** ```diet:[], time:null, kcal:null, costPP:null```<br/>**BRAAI HAS A COST.** `calcMeat` · `PORTION_BRAAI` · green food-cost · gold shop-spend. **SHE BUILT<br/>ALL OF IT. THE ADAPTER BINS IT ON THE WAY INTO THE INDEX.**<br/>🏆 **ONE LINE. FOUR FIELDS. THE WHOLE ROOM. That single line IS:**<br/>· **MF94-B** — Braai is dietary-blind *(92 recipes)*<br/>· **MF99** — no time on the search card<br/>· **the BUDGET BLINDNESS** — 92 recipes I\'ve Got R100 can never offer her<br/>**SAME SHAPE at `beverages` (354) · `tiny` (368) · `spice` (382) · `furry` (401).**<br/>⚠️ **A `health` adapter at :209 looks the same BUT health measures 100% costed — so that path is<br/>different or unused.** ⚖️ **Law 22 — CODE MUST CONFIRM, NOT ASSUME.**<br/><br/>⚖️ **LAW 23 — TWO BUGS SHARING A NAME DO NOT SHARE A FIX:**<br/>| 🔧 **Braai\'s binned cost** | **A BUG.** The data exists. One adapter line. | **AN AFTERNOON.** |<br/>| 📝 **The 998 unlabelled diets** | **CONTENT.** Derived in Node from ingredients. | **A MARATHON.** |<br/>| 📝 **The 532 missing costs** | **PARTLY CONTENT.** *A chutney may correctly have no cost.* | **A RULING, THEN A MARATHON.** |<br/><br/>🏆 **RULED BY TINA, 14 JUL:** 🐕 **PET FOOD IS COSTED.** · 🍹 **BEVERAGES ARE DELIBERATELY NOT<br/>COSTED** *(liquor is uncostable — 100s of gins and beers. Revisit if Grocify happens.)* ·<br/>**EVERYTHING ELSE MUST HAVE A PRICE.**<br/><br/>🩸 **⚖️ LAW 22 FIRED ON TINA\'S OWN MEMORY:** *she thought pet food was already costed.*<br/>**`furry.js` HAS ZERO COST FIELDS.** *(What she remembers is PRICE_DB — adding cheap INGREDIENTS<br/>because pet-food ingredients priced out dear. That work was real. It NEVER reached the recipes.)*<br/>✅ **AND THAT IS GOOD NEWS — NOBODY HAS TO RESEARCH 62 PRICES. `costRecipe()` + PRICE_DB<br/>CAN DO IT AUTOMATICALLY.** ⚖️ **Law 35.**<br/><br/>📏 **MEASURED — CAN `costRecipe()` PRICE EACH ROOM *TODAY*? *(does it have QUANTITIES?)***<br/>| 🌍 **world** | **88** | ✅ **AN AFTERNOON** — `{n:\'lamb\', pp:150, u:\'g\'}`. Priceable NOW. |<br/>| 🐕 **furry** | **62** | ✅ **AN AFTERNOON** — `{n:\'Pumpkin purée\', pp:200, u:\'g\'}` |<br/>| 👶 **tiny** | **18** | ✅ **AN AFTERNOON** |<br/>| 🔥 **braai** | **92** | ⚠️ **the amounts hide IN THE NAME:** *\'Boerewors — 350g per person solo…\'*<br/>   **+ `calcMeat` · `PORTION_BRAAI` ALREADY COMPUTE IT. THE ADAPTER NEVER ASKS.** |<br/>| 🎉 **events** | **22** | ⚠️ amounts must be written |<br/>| 🍹 **beverages** | **66** | ✅ **RULED — NOT COSTED.** *(Negroni → `{n:\'Gin\', pp:null}`. She was right.)* |<br/>| 🧂 **SPICE** | **184** | 💀 **NO INGREDIENT LIST AT ALL. → THIS IS THE MARATHON.** |<br/><br/>🩸🩸 **AND SPICE IS MF86 — ONE ROOT, FOUR SYMPTOMS.** *(`index.js:~384` writes `ingredients:[]`<br/>BY HAND. All 190 spice recipes are NAME-ONLY.)*<br/>· 🧂 **cannot be COSTED** *(184)*<br/>· 🧅 **INVISIBLE TO 4 INGREDIENTS** — she searches a fridge, Spice never answers<br/>· 🔍 **INVISIBLE TO INGREDIENT SEARCH** — *does `coriander` find Garam Masala?* **NO.**<br/>· 🥬 **CANNOT HAVE DIET TAGS DERIVED** — tags come from ingredients<br/>🏆 **190 INGREDIENT LISTS. THAT IS THE REAL WORK. EVERYTHING ELSE IS AFTERNOONS.**<br/><br/>🚨 **⚖️ LAW 45 HAS A SHARP EDGE HERE:** *\'we CHOSE not to cost this\'* and *\'we FORGOT to cost this\'*<br/>**ARE BOTH `costPP:null` RIGHT NOW. The budget tool cannot tell them apart and drops BOTH<br/>SILENTLY. BEVERAGES MUST SAY \'NOT COSTED\' OUT LOUD — NOT VANISH.** ⚖️ **Law 3.**"]"]
  end

