  subgraph LATER["🇿🇦 **PARKED — AFTER THE BUGS**"]
    L1["🏆 **'TINZA SPEAKS ENGLISH. BUT SHE UNDERSTANDS AFRIKAANS.'**<br/>⚖️ **Law 6 — it is the SAME map as MF88's ingredient brain. Build it once, and typing, categories<br/>AND voice all work.** 📊 **3404 ingredient names — but the top 50 cover everything a person types<br/>into a fridge box. ~200 words. A Saturday.** *(sout · botter · ui · knoffel · koekmeel · eier · melk …)*<br/>🎙️ **VOICE:** 🩸 **NOBODY SAYS 'chicken' IN A PRETORIA KITCHEN. SHE SAYS HOENDER.**<br/>**The mic is free in the browser (`af-ZA`). Voice is just TEXT through the same normaliser. A day.**<br/>💰 **A MOAT: NYT Cooking, at R49.99, WILL NEVER SPEAK AFRIKAANS.**<br/><br/>🧘 **THE RETREAT / CATERING PLANNER — PARKED. A DIFFERENT PRODUCT.**<br/>*(Wholesum already serves camps, retreat centres and personal chefs.)* 🩸 **Multi-person planning<br/>needs REAL-TIME SHARED STATE — a server, accounts, sync — or the sharing is FAKE.<br/>That is not `localStorage`. That is a backend.** **BUT it is literally Tina's trade. One day.**"]
