  subgraph LAW["⚖️ THE LAW — EVERY CLAUSE WAS PAID FOR"]
    Z1["1. **node --check PROVES NOTHING.** 2. **A REPORT IS NOT PROOF. HER FINGERS ON LIVE CLOSE IT.**<br/>3. 🩸 **SILENT WRONG IS WORSE THAN LOUD MISSING.** *(MF90.)*<br/>4. 🏆 **ASK 'WHAT IS NOT GUARDED?' — NEVER 'is X guarded?'** *(Turned ONE bug into a census of<br/>   SEVEN tools. She walked one. FOUR were broken.)*<br/>5. **ONE THING PER COMMIT. AND GIVE THE COMMIT A NAME.**<br/>6. **DON'T PATCH N SITES. BUILD THE ONE THING THEY SHOULD ALL CALL.** *(MF91: the price is<br/>   hard-coded 20 times. It should be ONE constant.)*<br/>10. **THE BUG IS IN THE DATA, NOT THE CODE.** 11. **NO MODEL AUTHORS A PRICE — OR A NAME.**<br/>15. 🩸 **A RULING THAT LIVES ONLY IN THE CHAT IS NOT A RULING.** *(R90 was ruled 28 JUNE and<br/>   vanished. Memory said R50 for TWO WEEKS. This law was written in blood and it still bit us.)*<br/>20. **A CARD THAT PRICES SOME OF THE FOOD IS WORSE THAN ONE THAT PRICES NONE.**<br/>   🆕 **AND: THE CACHE IS NOT A SHORTCUT. IT IS THE BUSINESS MODEL. NEVER RESET IT.**<br/>22. 🩸 **THE BRIEF IS A HYPOTHESIS, NOT EVIDENCE.** *(Fired again 13 Jul: Claude warned a reset<br/>   would 'delete her meal plan.' **THE MEAL PLANNER IS A COMING-SOON PAGE. HE NEVER READ IT.**)*<br/>23. **TWO BUGS SHARING A NAME DO NOT SHARE A FIX.**<br/>26. **IF THE CODE KNOWS IT AT WRITE-TIME, STORING IT IS NOT A FEATURE.**<br/>27. **PUBLISHED ≠ WHAT HER BROWSER IS RUNNING.** 28. **FURNITURE IS NOT CONTENT.**<br/>29. **A COMPLETE WORD HAS NO NEXT LETTER.** 30. **A CROSS-LINK IS CONTENT ABOUT ANOTHER DISH.**<br/>31. 🩸 **RENDER IT EMPTY ON THE WAY IN — don't clear it on the way out.** *(MF89.)*<br/>32. ***STRUCK.*** 33. **FOLLOW THE PATHS TO WHERE THEY CONVERGE.**<br/>34. **A ROOM NOBODY COULD REACH IS A ROOM NOBODY MAINTAINED.** *(Spice never got v33.)*<br/>35. 🏆 **STEP 1 IS 'READ', AND IT IS ALLOWED TO END THE TASK.** *(It turned MF89 from 'build a<br/>   clearing system' into 'add one missing string'.)* **EVERY BRIEF SHIPS WITH A STOP-CONDITION.**<br/>36. 🏆 **THE COUNT IS TRUTH. THE RENDER IS A COURTESY.**<br/>37. **DON'T PAINT A ROOM YOU ARE ABOUT TO DEMOLISH — but CHECK you are demolishing it.**<br/>38. 🏆 **A TOKEN CARD HAS NO COLOUR OF ITS OWN. IT INHERITS.**<br/>39. 🏆 **A TOOL RESULT IS ALSO A HYPOTHESIS. CROSS-CHECK IT WITH YOUR EYES.**<br/>40. 🏆 **`|| []` DOES NOT CATCH AN UNDECLARED NAME. IT THROWS — and an async throw VANISHES.**<br/>41. 🏆 **A MATCH OF 2-OF-4 IS NOT A MATCH. IT IS A COINCIDENCE. THE THRESHOLD IS THE FEATURE.**<br/>42. 🏆 **THE RATCHET — EVERY BUG YOU CLOSE ADDS A CHECK TO THE DOCTOR.**<br/>43. 🏆 **A MODEL MAY NOT BEND A DISH TO FIT THE FRIDGE. A BOBOTIE HAS NO POTATO IN IT —<br/>   NOT EVEN IF SHE HAS A POTATO.** ✅ **HELD ON LIVE, 13 JUL. FOUR HONEST NAMES. NOT ONE STOLEN.**<br/><br/>⛔ **44 — PROPOSED, NOT YET RULED:** 🆕 **A LOCK MUST HAVE SOMETHING BEHIND IT.**<br/>   **NEVER SELL A PADLOCK ON AN EMPTY ROOM.** *(MF92. Awaiting Tina.)*<br/>⚖️ **45 —** 🩸 **UNKNOWN IS NOT NO. AN UNTAGGED RECIPE IS NOT A<br/>   NON-VEGETARIAN RECIPE.** *(998 untagged recipes are being silently filtered OUT as if they<br/>   contained meat. A chutney is not a steak. MF94-B.)*<br/>🏆 **45 · 46 · 47 · 48 — RULED BY TINA, 14 JULY 2026. ALL FOUR. AS WRITTEN. THEY ARE LAW.** ⚖️ **Law 15.**<br/>⚖️ **47 —** 🩸 **A DIET IS A FACT, NOT A WORD IN A SENTENCE. NEVER MATCH A<br/>   DIET AGAINST PROSE.** *(A version's `feel` said 'the much-loved vegetarian…' — so a VEGAN was<br/>   handed a LAMB TAGINE. MF94-E.)*<br/>⚖️ **48 —** 🩸 **VEGAN IS A KIND OF VEGETARIAN. DIET IS A LADDER,<br/>   NOT A ROW OF BOXES.** *(199 vegan recipes are excluded from the vegetarian filter. MF94-D.)*<br/>⚖️ **46 —** 🩸 **ONE FOOD, ONE WORD. TWO ROOMS THAT TAG THE SAME FOOD<br/>   WITH DIFFERENT WORDS DO NOT HAVE A FILTER — THEY HAVE TWO FILTERS THAT DISAGREE.**<br/>   *(`veg` in FMF · `vegetarian` in World Kitchen. 48 vegetarian meals invisible. MF94-A.)*<br/><br/>📌 **PUSH RULE: '1 changed file' → PUSH. '0 changed files' → NOTHING TO PUSH. The screen never lies.**<br/>📌 **STANDING: Node `fs.writeFileSync`, NEVER Python · core.js = 4149 — count before and after.**"]
  end

